
==============================================================================
B3-1 CLOSURE GIVEN SEED: is (D, A_seed) -> A_closure unique?
==============================================================================
  [classical, earned class] closure = observable (Krylov) subspace of (K, c); computed two independent ways
  generic weighted net, generic seed: dim 24 (Krylov) / 24 (spectral); span gap 2.5e-15; frame covariance gap 2.9e-15
  C1-a path, end-site seed e1 (earned readout): dim 24 (Krylov) / 24 (spectral); span gap 2.8e-15; frame covariance gap 2.8e-15
  C1-a path, reflection-symmetric seed e1 + e24 (symmetry-reducible): dim 12 (Krylov) / 12 (spectral); span gap 5.4e-14; frame covariance gap 4.4e-14
  decoupled (abelian) control: K diagonal, seed e1 + e2: dim 2 (Krylov) / 2 (spectral); span gap 2.8e-16; frame covariance gap 8.4e-15
  -> classical closure is a definite function of (K, seed): unique, method-independent, frame-covariant.
     symmetric seed closes on the reflection-even block (dim N/2); decoupled control closes on the seed's modes only.

  [auxiliary quantum class] three closure RULES appear in the canonical record:
     R_P5 = alg{I, H, B} (P-5 instrument);  R_P6 = unital *-alg of seed, ad_H-closed (P-6 closure, adh=True);
     R_static = unital *-alg of seed, no dynamics (P-6 L-D2 sufficiency, adh=False)
  generic H, seed sx1: dims R_P5 16, R_P6 16, R_static 2; rule-internal reproducibility gaps 1.0e-15 / 9.6e-16; center dims 1 / 1
  parity-symmetric H ([H, z1z2] = 0), seed sz1: dims R_P5 8, R_P6 8, R_static 2; rule-internal reproducibility gaps 5.6e-16 / 3.9e-16; center dims 2 / 2
  abelian: diagonal H, diagonal seed: dims R_P5 4, R_P6 4, R_static 4; rule-internal reproducibility gaps 3.5e-16 / 3.6e-16; center dims 4 / 4
  site 1 DECOUPLED from a 2-spin hidden sector, seed sx1: dims R_P5 16, R_P6 4, R_static 2; rule-internal reproducibility gaps 8.2e-15 / 2.5e-16; center dims 4 / 1
  representation control (R_P6): cl(VSV^+; VHV^+) vs V cl(S;H) V^+ gap 1.5e-15
  -> GIVEN a closure rule, the closure is unique (reproducible, covariant). ACROSS the rules the canonical record uses,
     the closure of the same (H, seed) differs when H has structure outside the seed's reach (decoupled-hidden case):
     the closure rule is itself a declared convention (R_P5 imports H into the access algebra).

==============================================================================
B3-2 SAME D, SAME Sigma, different seeds: identical closure / central structure, different downstream physics?
==============================================================================
  [classical, earned class] same K (and same net), single-site seeds
  C1-a path N=24 (unit springs): cyclic (informationally complete) single sites 16/24; all have IDENTICAL closure (R^N, trivial center);
     pairs 120: transfer-function-identical pairs 8 (automorphism / gauge); physically DISTINCT pairs 112; e1 vs e24 max|dG| = 4.58e-16
  weighted path N=24 (L0-1b-type, asymmetric weights): cyclic (informationally complete) single sites 24/24; all have IDENTICAL closure (R^N, trivial center);
     pairs 276: transfer-function-identical pairs 0 (automorphism / gauge); physically DISTINCT pairs 276; e1 vs e24 max|dG| = 1.43e-01

  [auxiliary quantum class] 3-spin chain 1-2-3, parity P = z1z2z3 conserved, seeds sz1 vs sz3 (P-6 L-B, re-implemented, new H)
   trial 0: [H,P] 0e+00; R_P6 dims 32/32 gap 1.3e-15, center 2/2; R_P5 dims 32/32 gap 2.1e-15; probe coherence max diff 0.673
   trial 1: [H,P] 0e+00; R_P6 dims 32/32 gap 1.3e-15, center 2/2; R_P5 dims 32/32 gap 2.0e-15; probe coherence max diff 0.516
   trial 2: [H,P] 0e+00; R_P6 dims 32/32 gap 1.4e-15, center 2/2; R_P5 dims 32/32 gap 1.9e-15; probe coherence max diff 0.555
  Sigma check: the net (chain 1-2-3 / path) is IDENTICAL for both seeds and both are END sites of it, so Sigma's
  graph role cannot separate them; any rule that does (e.g. 'the end with larger field') is an added criterion.

