B3-3 informational completeness vs readout selection (classical Level-0)
==============================================================================
  C1-a N=24: single-site readouts that are informationally complete (full observability rank): 16; not: [1, 4, 7, 10, 13, 16, 19, 22] (sites, 0-based)
  random linear functionals h(x) = c.x: informationally complete 200/200
  end sites e1, e24 (symmetry orbit): max|dG| 4.6e-16 -> GAUGE pair; e1 vs e6 max|dG| 0.510 -> different physics
  -> READOUT COMPLETENESS != READOUT SELECTION: completeness holds for an open dense set of readouts, which differ physically.

