B3-4 GS1 inverse: given the SAME K / Sigma / geometry, is the access boundary reconstructable?
==============================================================================
  full site-resolved: observability rank 9/9; static response trace 6.576; full-access K reconstruction error 1.3e-15
  boundary {0,2,8}: observability rank 9/9; static response trace 2.441
  other 3-set {1,3,5}: observability rank 9/9; static response trace 2.065
  single site {0}: observability rank 9/9; static response trace 0.812
  single site {4}: observability rank 9/9; static response trace 0.596
  admissible informationally complete boundaries on the SAME K: singletons 9/9, 3-sets 84/84
  candidate inverse selectors: max-information -> the full set (monotone: any superset dominates; never the declared boundary);
  min-cardinality complete -> 9 tied singletons; GS1-selection power -> full access only. None returns a given declared boundary.
  -> GS1 IS ONE-WAY: declared access -> geometry, not geometry -> access.

