B3-7 resolution / hierarchy order: is a final finite truncation fixed by D?
==============================================================================
  hidden edge (3,4) changed: end-site Markov moments agree through order 31, first differ at order 32; max transfer difference 3.24e-03
  hidden edge (6,7) changed: end-site Markov moments agree through order 34, first differ at order 35; max transfer difference 1.26e-04
  hidden edge (10,11) changed: end-site Markov moments agree through order 39, first differ at order 40; max transfer difference 1.66e-06
  resolution threshold delta = 1e-02: perturbed edges detectable at the end site 2/23 (deepest detectable edge 1)
  resolution threshold delta = 1e-04: perturbed edges detectable at the end site 7/23 (deepest detectable edge 6)
  resolution threshold delta = 1e-06: perturbed edges detectable at the end site 11/23 (deepest detectable edge 10)
  resolution threshold delta = 1e-08: perturbed edges detectable at the end site 15/23 (deepest detectable edge 14)
  -> sufficiency is order- and threshold-relative; the required order / delta is set by the unknown alternative, not by D.

==============================================================================
B3-8 path-dependent minimality (classical re-implementation of the P-6 L-D2 logic)
==============================================================================
  uniform 5x5 grid: degenerate eigenvalue pairs 11 -> no single readout is complete (needs >= 2 outputs)
  pool (first lexicographic 5-site pool with differing outcomes) (0, 1, 2, 3, 4): forward elimination -> [1, 2, 3, 4], reverse -> [0, 1, 2, 3]; both sufficient AND minimal: True / True
  all minimal sufficient subsets of this pool: [(0, 1, 2, 3), (0, 1, 2, 4), (0, 1, 3, 4), (0, 2, 3, 4), (1, 2, 3, 4)]
  -> MINIMALITY DOES NOT SELECT A_seed (path-dependent; several minimal sets).

