B3-9 / B3-10 fragment grouping and temporal access (same net, same D; 'how many fragments record site 12?')
==============================================================================
  record criterion: posterior variance of x_12(0) (prior 1) from noisy samples (sigma 1e-3) of the fragment, below threshold
  horizon T= 1.0, cadence dt=0.5, threshold var<0.6: single sites (24): 1/24; adjacent pairs (12): 2/12; blocks of 6 (4): 2/4
  horizon T= 1.0, cadence dt=0.5, threshold var<0.3: single sites (24): 1/24; adjacent pairs (12): 1/12; blocks of 6 (4): 2/4
  horizon T= 5.0, cadence dt=0.5, threshold var<0.6: single sites (24): 3/24; adjacent pairs (12): 5/12; blocks of 6 (4): 2/4
  horizon T= 5.0, cadence dt=0.5, threshold var<0.3: single sites (24): 1/24; adjacent pairs (12): 3/12; blocks of 6 (4): 2/4
  horizon T=20.0, cadence dt=2.0, threshold var<0.6: single sites (24): 1/24; adjacent pairs (12): 2/12; blocks of 6 (4): 2/4
  horizon T=20.0, cadence dt=2.0, threshold var<0.3: single sites (24): 0/24; adjacent pairs (12): 0/12; blocks of 6 (4): 0/4
  D's own timescales: slowest relaxation rate 0.30, fastest 4.28 -- units, not a schedule
  -> the 'record redundancy' count changes with grouping, horizon, cadence and threshold; nothing in K or the net selects them.
